  "name": "3. The GM Sets the Position",
  "slug": "6-4-3-the-gm-sets-the-position",
  "source": {
    "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/fitd-system-json/objects/sources/blades-in-the-dark-srd"
  },
  "sourceLocator": {
    "chapter": "Action Roll",
    "section": "6.4",
    "heading": "3. The GM Sets the Position",
    "lineStart": 330,
    "lineEnd": 334
  },
  "section": "6.4",
  "rulesText": "Once the player chooses their action, the GM sets the **position** for the roll. The position represents how dangerous or troublesome the action might be. There are three positions: **controlled**, **risky**, and **desperate**. To choose a position, the GM looks at the profiles for the positions below and picks one that most closely matches the situation at hand.\n\n**By default, an action roll is risky.** You wouldn't be rolling if there was no risk involved. If the situation seems more dangerous, make it desperate. If it seems less dangerous, make it controlled."
}
